Drought and heatwaves have pushed French winegrowers to start picking grapes weeks ahead of schedule, with this year seeing some of the earliest harvests on record – a sign of how climate change is reshaping the wine calendar across the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31807718-9a4f-11f1-af8a-39f218d346d1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 04:41:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg">© Sarah Meyssonnier/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>July heatwave sees 1,243 deaths in France, bringing summer toll to 7,300</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260820-july-heatwave-caused-over-1-200-deaths-in-france-bringing-summer-toll-to-7-300</link><description>
